# inc-qaav4: wield the unholy Nine Lives Stealer ONCE on a loaded wrong-alignment (Chaotic Good)
# character and photograph what follows. Used with the level 1 fixture (the wield must kill him)
# and the level 2 fixture (he must live at 0 effective XP). Read by tools/check_alignment_drain_edges.sh.
#
# Dumps: sheet-0-baseline before the wield; wield-prompt right after it (the message line shows
# "uneasy", and "You die... Die? [yn]" when the wield kills him); sheet-1-after after it. A dead
# character cannot open the sheet, so on the level 1 fixture sheet-1-after still shows the prompt.
s
d
@expect "Align  Chaotic Good"
@dump:sheet-0-baseline
ESC
w
@choose "Genocide Everything"
w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*10
@until "Nine Lives Stealer" DOWN
DOWN
ENTER
2
ENTER
b
SPACE
@dump:wield-prompt
@while "two-handed" n
s
ESC
d
@dump:sheet-1-after
ESC
